  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "kt_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -304
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Kaleidoscope Toy\n\nA real kaleidoscope: loose beads tumbling in a round chamber, seen through mirrors. Drag sideways to turn the tube — gravity turns with it and the beads slide and tumble — and beads trickle in where you press. Keys 3–9 set the number of mirrors, C empties the chamber. Left alone it turns slowly by itself.\n\nHow it works: an Emitter's beads live in a World whose gravity points 'down the tube' (a vector rotated by the Turn) and whose inverted Circle collider keeps them in the chamber. Symmetry in kaleidoscope mode mirrors that layer into the wedges, turned with the tube; a Mask rounds the view off and Effect bloom makes the glass glow.",
        "width": 460,
        "height": 240
      }
    },
